INT. DEFUNCT CLOCK TOWER - GEAR ROOM - NIGHT

A cathedral of brass wheels and iron pendulums, stilled for thirty years. Moonlight comes through the huge translucent dial and paints the room the color of old ivory.

Two men in dark clothes work their way along a catwalk above the great gear train. TOBIAS FENWICK-ADEYEMI (50s, gray stubble, a coil of rope on his shoulder) goes first. MATTHEW "MATT" ROSALES-HEIDT (30s, gloves, a backpack heavy with tools) follows.

They stop at a small iron door set into the wall behind the largest wheel.

TOBIAS
That's the vault.

MATT
It's a clock.

TOBIAS
The clockmaker's safe. Eighteen-ninety-two. Built into the movement itself.

MATT
How do you know?

TOBIAS
Because I read the blueprints, Matt. All eleven hundred pages.

Matt swings his pack off. Kneels in front of the door. Tobias holds a flashlight over his shoulder.

MATT
Hold it steady.

TOBIAS
I am holding it steady.

MATT
You're breathing on it.

TOBIAS
You're bending the beam.

Matt looks up. Tobias lowers the light. A small, wary silence. Then Matt starts work, the picks clicking softly in the lock.

MATT
Tobias, if he sees him standing in the light like that...

TOBIAS
Who?

MATT
Him. The one you hired to watch the street.

TOBIAS
I hired nobody.

MATT
Then who's in the street?

Tobias goes still. Matt goes still. Each waits for the other to say it.

The lock gives. The door swings open on a velvet-lined compartment. Inside, a single pocket watch on a gold chain, ticking.

MATT (CONT'D)
It's running.

TOBIAS
It shouldn't be.

Far below, with a groan like a waking giant, the great gear train begins to turn. He grabs the rail. He grabs the rope. Neither of them can tell which of them is shouting.
